abstract: >-
  Engine and experiments of the Endolexis theory: the outside world is the dictionary with which a mind
  reads its own inside. Includes the stage engine of "Olvasó: an entity that reads itself" and, from
  version 0.2.0, endolexis.toyworld, a toy-world Olvasó with experiments on temperament, forgetting and
  doubt, sealed sleep and dream recall, and a response to "Language Models Need Sleep" (consolidation and
  dreaming). Version 0.3.0 adds toy world v1, the symbiote: a room seen, heard and touched through processor
  entities, a vocabulary per processor, actions through a guard, and the auditory and visual mirror tests
  (experiments 12-15).
